In searching the origin of the transverse single spin asymmetry, one particularly interesting way is through the topological dependence of \(\pi^{0}\) TSSAs. It refers to dividing the \(\pi^{0}\) sample into two groups based on the \(\pi^{0}\) event struc

Figure 4.13: Combined results of the TSSA of only the \(\pi^{0}\) signal at \(x_{F}\) in Run-11 and Run-15 at overlapped \(x_{F}\) region.

